From: Apple-on-Virt Project
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] target/arm: Add Apple-specific ARM64 system registers

This patch adds stub implementations for Apple-specific ARM64 system
registers required by XNU kernel. These registers are not part of
the standard ARM architecture but are expected by macOS/Darwin.

Registers added:
- HID3, HID4, HID5, HID7, HID8, HID11 (Hardware Implementation Defined)
- EHID1, EHID4, EHID10 (Extended HID)
- LSU_ERR_STS (Load/Store Unit Error Status)
- PMC0, PMC1, PMCR1, PMSR (Performance Monitor Control)
- APRR_EL0, APRR_EL1 (Apple Page Region Protection)
- CTRR registers (Configurable Text Region Range)
- Other Apple-specific registers

All registers are implemented as read/write storage that accept any
value and return the last written value (or 0 as default).

Signed-off-by: Apple-on-Virt Project
---
